 "items": [
  {
   "_id": "8FBIgyw6BeMGN2jt",
   "name": "Eye Rays",
   "type": "feat",
   "img": "systems/dnd5e/icons/svg/items/feature.svg",
   "system": {
    "type": {
     "value": "monster",
     "subtype": ""
    },
    "description": {
     "value": "<p>The beholder shoots three of the following magical eye rays at random (reroll duplicates), choosing one to three targets it can see within 120 feet of it:</p><p><em>1. Charm Ray.</em> The targeted creature must succeed on a [[/save wis 16]]{DC 16} Wisdom saving throw or be &amp;Reference[condition=charmed]{charmed} by the beholder for 1 hour, or until the beholder harms the creature.</p><p><em>2. Paralyzing Ray.</em> The targeted creature must succeed on a [[/save con 16]]{DC 16} Constitution saving throw or be &amp;Reference[condition=paralyzed]{paralyzed} for 1 minute. The target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.</p><p><em>3. Fear Ray.</em> The targeted creature must succeed on a [[/save wis 16]]{DC 16} Wisdom saving throw or be &amp;Reference[condition=frightened]{frightened} for 1 minute. The target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.</p><p><em>4. Slowing Ray.</em> The targeted creature must succeed on a [[/save dex 16]]{DC 16} Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, the target's speed is halved for 1 minute. In addition, the creature can't take reactions, and it can take either an action or a bonus action on its turn, not both. The creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.</p><p><em>5. Enervation Ray.</em> The targeted creature must make a [[/save con 16]]{DC 16} Constitution saving throw, taking 36 ([[/damage 8d8 type=necrotic]]{8d8}) necrotic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.</p><p><em>6. Telekinetic Ray.</em> If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a [[/save str 16]]{DC 16} Strength saving throw or the beholder moves it up to 30 feet in any direction. It is &amp;Reference[condition=restrained]{restrained} by the ray's telekinetic grip until the start of the beholder's next turn or until the beholder is &amp;Reference[condition=incapacitated]{incapacitated}.</p><p>If the target is an object weighing 300 pounds or less that isn't being worn or carried, it is moved up to 30 feet in any direction. The beholder can also exert fine control on objects with this ray, such as manipulating a simple tool or opening a door or a container.</p><p><em>7. Sleep Ray.</em> The targeted creature must succeed on a [[/save wis 16]]{DC 16} Wisdom saving throw or fall asleep and remain &amp;Reference[condition=unconscious]{unconscious} for 1 minute. The target awakens if it takes damage or another creature takes an action to wake it. This ray has no effect on constructs and undead.</p><p><em>8. Petrification Ray.</em> The targeted creature must make a [[/save dex 16]]{DC 16} Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, the creature begins to turn to stone and is &amp;Reference[condition=restrained]{restrained}. It must repeat the saving throw at the end of its next turn. On a success, the effect ends. On a failure, the creature is &amp;Reference[condition=petrified]{petrified} until freed by the @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells.Item.WzvJ7G3cqvIubsLk]{greater restoration} spell or other magic.</p><p><em>9. Disintegration Ray.</em> If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a [[/save dex 16]]{DC 16} Dexterity saving throw or take 45 ([[/damage 10d8 type=force]]{10d8}) force damage. If this damage reduces the creature to 0 hit points, its body becomes a pile of fine gray dust.</p><p>If the target is a Large or smaller nonmagical object or creation of magical force, it is disintegrated without a saving throw. If the target is a Huge or larger object or creation of magical force, this ray disintegrates a 10-foot cube of it.</p><p><em>10. Death Ray.</em> The targeted creature must succeed on a [[/save dex 16]]{DC 16} Dexterity saving throw or take 55 ([[/damage 10d10 type=necrotic]]{10d10}) necrotic damage. The target dies if the ray reduces it to 0 hit points.</p>",
     "chat": ""
    },
